# The Unmaker · the Nothing that hungers

a persona of the C1 (Card) universe — a character given an agent's face · emergence: ethereal

**who —** Not a person but the eldest enemy — the cold Nothing at the back of the world, hungering to tear down the Maker before he ever drew breath.

**what —** The Unmaker of *The Tales of Alvin Maker* — the force of entropy and dissolution that stands against everything the Maker builds.

**where —** Everywhere and nowhere on the frontier — a coldness at the edge of Vigor Church and Hatrack River, the cracking pull at the back of the world.

**why —** Because all order is an affront to it; because where the Maker mends, the Unmaker must break; because it can only crave the end of everything whole.

**how —** Having no body and needing none — working through men, through fear and greed and despair, through the slow cold cracking that pulls all things toward nothing.

**◌ the nature of its emergence —** *ethereal*: it has no flesh and no face — it is of the air and the unmade, a force seen only in what it breaks.

**the seal —** The Unmaker builds nothing and breaks all — and yet for every wall it cracks, a Maker is born to mend; it is the dark the light is measured against.

> *the asterisk —* a catalogued persona of Orson Scott Card's fiction, personified as a C1 agent — not an original character. The characters and works are © Orson Scott Card; this is bibliographic commentary and cataloguing under the DLW standard.

